## Summary

This is a Spring PetClinic (OfficeFloor variant) repo. All the logic you asked about lives in the owner "function" package: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`. Notably, **fiscal year is NOT implemented in `src/main`** — it exists only as an expectation in a test.

---

### 1. Membership identifier with a year segment derived from the registration date

**File:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipNumber.java` (full content, 18 lines)

The `membershipNumber` is formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where `YY` is the last two digits of the registration-date year:

```java
14	    public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
15	        String yy = String.format("%02d", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);
16	        owner.setMembershipNumber(owner.getCustomerCode() + "-M" + yy);
17	    }
